{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"The cache experiment shows that bypassing loads is counterproductive, while streaming stores provide only about a 1% gain. I’m also checking a lower-register schedule that completes query before loading key; if it preserves enough memory-level parallelism, the added occupancy can be more valuable than keeping both reductions live at once."}}
