{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"Pure head-major scheduling harms HBM locality at scale. I’m refining it into small local tiles—two to sixteen consecutive tokens per head, then moving to the next head—so weight reuse improves without turning the main tensor accesses into a globally strided stream."}}
